Z||000000||Greg Piet||12-17-2000||08:58 PM||||I know I SHOULD know this but...<P>As far as wheels go, I know it is a 5 bolt pattern.<P>What are the width of stock 14" and 15" wheels.<P>What is the offset?<P>I really want to be able to go to a Wheel/tire place and be sure to use the right terminology.<P>Reason:  I want to put 225/50/15 Hoosiers on the back (got a great source) but I want to put them on the proper rim.  I have a set of 15" rims that fit the Fiero, but I think they are 6" (like stock 14" width) and I think the 225's would have the sidewalls bow in too much which would reduce my contact patch(7" rims required).  If I know all the info needed for a rim purchase I can go price out what I exactly need.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-18-2000||10:15 AM||||The stock wheels are 14" X 6"<BR>86/87 15" X 7"<BR>88 15" X 6" on the front and 15" X 7" on the rear.<BR> Not sure of the offset. I think they are 38mm or 40mm. Bolt pattern is 5 X 100mm.<BR>As for tire size vs. wheels. According to the BFGoodrich tire chart, 6" is the minimum (8" max) recommended width for a 225/50R15. I have 225's on mine but they are on a 15X7 wheel.||||reg||1
